.TH NUDGE-BASH 1 "" "Nudge" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nudge-bash \- local-first command correction for Bash on Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nudge-bash
.I action
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Nudge suggests corrections after a failed command in an interactive Bash 5+
shell. Press Enter to accept a displayed correction; any other key cancels.
The executable name must be spelled correctly. Command support is scoped to
reviewed syntax and installed metadata. Shell expansions, pipelines, aliases,
functions, and builtins are not corrected.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B supported
List registered executable adapters. Registration does not imply all forms
of a command are supported.
.TP
.B refresh
Refresh command catalog metadata.
.TP
.B suggest
Return a suggestion as JSON without executing it.
.TP
.B confirm
Prompt for confirmation and emit the accepted argument vector for the Bash hook.
.TP
.B config
Show effective settings, or save provider, model, and endpoint options.
.TP
.B models
List models from the selected local model server.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --command " TEXT"
Failed command line to analyze.
.TP
.BI --status " CODE"
Original exit status (default 1). Successful and interrupted commands are skipped.
.TP
.B --local-only
Use deterministic corrections only.
.TP
.BI --provider " codex|claude|ollama|local"
Select optional Codex, Claude Code, or local LLM fallback.
.TP
.BI --model " ID"
Choose a model available through the selected backend.
.TP
.BI --endpoint " URL"
Set a loopback HTTP endpoint for a local model server.
.TP
.B --force-ai
Request a model for eligible adapters. Local-only adapter boundaries still apply.
.TP
.BR --help , " -h"
Show usage.
.TP
.BR --version , " -V"
Show the version.
.SH ACTIVATION
Add the following guarded line to your own Bash startup file for a system package:
.PP
.nf
[[ -r /usr/lib/nudge-bash/nudge.bash ]] && source /usr/lib/nudge-bash/nudge.bash
.fi
.PP
For a manual Makefile installation, substitute its prefix (default /usr/local).
Start a new Bash shell. Remove an earlier Nudge source line before enabling a
different installation. Package installation does not edit startup files.
.SH FILES
Configuration uses $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/nudge/config.json, or ~/.config/nudge/config.json.
Cache uses $XDG_CACHE_HOME/nudge, or ~/.cache/nudge.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
NUDGE_ENABLED=0 disables suggestions. NUDGE_LOCAL_ONLY=1 disables model fallback.
NUDGE_PROVIDER selects the backend. See PROVIDERS.md for model-specific settings.
Explicit options override environment variables, which override saved settings.
.SH MAINTENANCE
Use the package manager for package updates and removal. The per-user install,
uninstall, and rollback actions are unavailable from this installation.
User configuration and cache are retained when package files are removed.
